{"book":11,"chapter":4,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / THE JAVASCRIPT LANGUAGE / CHAPTER 4","slides":[{"title":"One Language — Everywhere","sub":"Chapter 4 · Browser and Server","short":"Introduction","main":"JavaScript is the only language in every browser; the same environment exists on the server.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Browser","Node.js","Client and server"],"captions":["JavaScript runs in every browser with no install: it brings the page to life","The same language runs on the server and the command line — in the Node.js environment, with files and processes","At the end of the book we write our own mini-framework: one language on client and server"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"js","x":180.0,"y":34.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"JavaScript","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"br","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":190.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Browser\npage, events, network","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"js","x":180.0,"y":34.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"JavaScript","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"br","x":100.0,"y":100.0,"w":150.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Browser\npage, events","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"nd","x":260.0,"y":100.0,"w":150.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Node.js\nfiles, processes, packages","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":150.0,"y1":48.0,"x2":118.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"a2","x1":210.0,"y1":48.0,"x2":242.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"js","x":180.0,"y":34.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"JavaScript","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"br","x":80.0,"y":100.0,"w":120.0,"h":40.0,"text":"client\nin the browser","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"nd","x":280.0,"y":100.0,"w":120.0,"h":40.0,"text":"server\non Node.js","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":142.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":218.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":80.0,"text":"HTTP / WebSocket","size":9.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[19.1,32.1]}]},{"title":"Engine","sub":"V8: parse, bytecode, JIT","short":"Engine","main":"Text → tree → bytecode → machine code for hot functions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Parsing","Bytecode","JIT compilation"],"captions":["The V8 engine reads the program text and parses it into a tree — like a compiler in other languages","The tree becomes bytecode, which the interpreter runs at once, with no long warm-up","Frequently called functions are compiled on the fly to machine code — this is JIT"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":56.0,"y":50.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"text","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":96.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":130.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":170.0,"y":50.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"parser","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":244.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":290.0,"y":50.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"AST tree","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":56.0,"y":50.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"text","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":96.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":130.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":170.0,"y":50.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"parser","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":244.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":290.0,"y":50.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"AST tree","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":290.0,"y1":68.0,"x2":130.0,"y2":112.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"bc","x":90.0,"y":120.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"bytecode","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":170.0,"y":50.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"parser","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":290.0,"y":50.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"AST tree","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"bc","x":90.0,"y":120.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"bytecode","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e4","x1":142.0,"y1":120.0,"x2":200.0,"y2":120.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":270.0,"y":120.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"machine code","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":94.0,"text":"for “hot” functions","size":9.0}]],"cues":[15.9,27.6]}]},{"title":"First program","sub":"console.log and templates","short":"console.log","main":"In the browser output goes to the DevTools console, in Node to the terminal.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["console.log","Running","Template string"],"captions":["console.log prints a value: in the browser to the developer tools console, in Node to the terminal","A file runs with the node command and its name; a page includes a script with the script tag","A string in backticks inserts expression values via ${…} right into the text"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["console.log(\"Hello, world!\");"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":18.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"browser: DevTools console · Node: terminal","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":28.0,"lines":["console.log(\"Hello, world!\");"],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":18.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":250.0,"h":44.0,"text":"$ node hello.js\nHello, world!","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":34.0,"lines":["const name = \"world\";","console.log(`Hello, ${name}!`);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"w":200.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Hello, world!","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[11.6,30.6]}]},{"title":"let, const, var","sub":"Declaring variables","short":"Variables","main":"const by default, let when the value changes; don't use var.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["let and const","const and objects","var — not needed"],"captions":["const creates a binding that can't be reassigned; let makes a variable whose value changes","const doesn't make an object immutable: replacing it is forbidden, but fields can change","var is visible in the whole function, not the block, and is “hoisted” — so it isn't used"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":34.0,"lines":["const PI = 3.14;","let count = 0;","count = count + 1;","PI = 3;  // TypeError"],"hl":[2],"bad":[3],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const user = { n: 1 };","user.n = 2;   // allowed","user = {};    // TypeError"],"hl":[1],"bad":[2],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["if (true) {","  var a = 1;","}","console.log(a);  // 1 — visible outside"],"bad":[3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":132.0,"text":"write const by default, and let when the value changes","size":9.0}]],"cues":[11.9,34.1]}]},{"title":"Value types","sub":"Seven primitives and typeof","short":"Types","main":"The value carries the type, not the variable; typeof null gives “object”.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Seven primitives","typeof","null and undefined"],"captions":["There are seven primitives: number, string, boolean, null, undefined, bigint and symbol; everything else is an object","typeof returns the type name; for null it gives “object” — a historical mistake, and an array is also “object”","undefined — no value set, null is set on purpose; the value carries the type, not the variable"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"p0","x":56.0,"y":50.0,"w":74.0,"h":30.0,"text":"number","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p1","x":138.0,"y":50.0,"w":74.0,"h":30.0,"text":"string","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p2","x":220.0,"y":50.0,"w":74.0,"h":30.0,"text":"boolean","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p3","x":302.0,"y":50.0,"w":74.0,"h":30.0,"text":"null","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"q0","x":98.0,"y":96.0,"w":74.0,"h":30.0,"text":"undefined","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"q1","x":180.0,"y":96.0,"w":74.0,"h":30.0,"text":"bigint","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"q2","x":262.0,"y":96.0,"w":74.0,"h":30.0,"text":"symbol","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":146.0,"text":"objects: arrays, functions, Date …","size":9.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":34.0,"lines":["typeof 42       // \"number\"","typeof \"a\"      // \"string\"","typeof null     // \"object\" !","typeof []       // \"object\""],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"u","x":100.0,"y":46.0,"w":140.0,"h":36.0,"text":"undefined\nvalue not set","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n~cell","x":260.0,"y":46.0,"w":140.0,"h":36.0,"text":"null\nempty on purpose","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":90.0,"lines":["let a;         // undefined","let b = null;  // no value","b = 7; b = 's';  // the value has the type"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":290.0}]],"cues":[18.9,30.0]}]},{"title":"Numbers","sub":"IEEE 754, NaN, BigInt","short":"Numbers","main":"There is one number type, floating-point; BigInt is for exact large integers.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Floating-point","Safe integers","NaN and BigInt"],"captions":["There is always one number type — a double, 64-bit IEEE 754, so 0.1 + 0.2 isn't equal to 0.3","Integers are exact only up to 2 to the 53rd power: beyond it, neighboring numbers start to merge","NaN isn't even equal to itself; for exact large integers there is BigInt, with an n at the end"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["0.1 + 0.2          // 0.30000000000000004","0.1 + 0.2 === 0.3  // false"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"like double in C: 64 bits, 52 of them mantissa","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":44.0,"w":280.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER = 9007199254740991","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":90.0,"lines":["2 ** 53 === 2 ** 53 + 1   // true","// beyond the limit numbers merge"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["NaN === NaN     // false","1 / 0           // Infinity","10n ** 20n      // 100000000000000000000n","10n + 1         // TypeError"],"hl":[0],"bad":[3],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[13.4,29.9]}]},{"title":"Strings","sub":"UTF-16 and methods","short":"Strings","main":"Strings are immutable; for-of walks over characters, not units.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["UTF-16","Characters and units","Methods"],"captions":["A string is stored in UTF-16: an emoji takes two 16-bit units, so its length is two","Indexes and length count units, while for-of walks over real characters","Strings are immutable: every method — slice, split, includes, trim — returns a new string"],"frames":[[{"t":"text","id":"e","x":180.0,"y":30.0,"text":"😀","size":22.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":130.0,"y":86.0,"w":76.0,"h":32.0,"text":"D83D","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":230.0,"y":86.0,"w":76.0,"h":32.0,"text":"DE00","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"two UTF-16 units → length = 2","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["'😀'.length        // 2","[...'😀'].length   // 1","for (const ch of s) {","  console.log(ch);","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["s.slice(0, 3)","s.split(' ')","s.includes('ab')","s.trim()"],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":160.0},{"t":"cell","id":"n~cell","x":280.0,"y":74.0,"w":130.0,"h":44.0,"text":"each call —\na new string","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e~line","x1":200.0,"y1":74.0,"x2":212.0,"y2":74.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[15.8,31.5]}]},{"title":"Truthy and falsy","sub":"||, ?? and ?.","short":"Truthy","main":"Six values are falsy; ?? reacts only to null and undefined.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Six falsy values","|| and ??","The ?. chain"],"captions":["Six values are falsy: false, 0, the empty string, null, undefined and NaN; the rest is truthy, even []","|| returns the first “truthy” operand, while ?? picks the right one only for null and undefined","The ?. chain walks safely through nested fields: on an empty value it stops and gives undefined"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"f0","x":40.0,"y":56.0,"w":52.0,"h":28.0,"text":"false","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f1","x":96.0,"y":56.0,"w":52.0,"h":28.0,"text":"0","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f2","x":152.0,"y":56.0,"w":52.0,"h":28.0,"text":"\"\"","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f3","x":208.0,"y":56.0,"w":52.0,"h":28.0,"text":"null","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f4","x":264.0,"y":56.0,"w":52.0,"h":28.0,"text":"undefined","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f5","x":320.0,"y":56.0,"w":52.0,"h":28.0,"text":"NaN","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"everything else is truthy:  []  {}  '0'  -1","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["'' || 'default'   // 'default'","0 ?? 5               // 0","null ?? 5            // 5"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["user?.profile?.name","// undefined, not TypeError"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":118.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"user","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":106.0,"y1":118.0,"x2":144.0,"y2":118.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"profile","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":216.0,"y1":118.0,"x2":254.0,"y2":118.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":290.0,"y":118.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"undefined","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[18.3,29.1]}]},{"title":"Loops","sub":"for, for…of, for…in","short":"Loops","main":"For collections — for…of; for…in goes over property names.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["for","for…of","for…in"],"captions":["The familiar three-part for, while and do-while, plus break and continue, work as in C","for…of yields array values, string characters, set elements — usually what you want","for…in goes over property names as strings: for arrays that is almost always a mistake"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {","  console.log(i);   // 0, 1, 2","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for (const x of ['a', 'b']) {","  console.log(x);   // 'a', 'b'","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["for (const k in ['a', 'b']) {","  console.log(k);   // '0', '1'","}"],"hl":[0],"bad":[0],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"property names, as strings","tone":"red","size":9.5}]],"cues":[12.5,29.0]}]},{"title":"Values and references","sub":"Heap and garbage collector","short":"References","main":"Primitives are copied, objects are passed by reference.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Copy of a value","Reference to an object","Garbage collector"],"captions":["Primitives are copied by value: after let b = a the variables are independent","Objects and arrays live in the heap, the variable holds a reference: a change through one is visible through the other","The garbage collector takes objects unreachable from the roots; there is no ownership as in Rust"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":40.0,"text":"a\n5","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":260.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":40.0,"text":"b\n5","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":138.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":222.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"let b = a — a copy of the number","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":60.0,"y":40.0,"w":60.0,"h":36.0,"text":"x\nref","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"y","x":60.0,"y":100.0,"w":60.0,"h":36.0,"text":"y\nref","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":40.0,"text":"{ n: 1 }\nin the heap","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":92.0,"y1":42.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":62.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":92.0,"y1":98.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":78.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":60.0,"y":40.0,"w":60.0,"h":36.0,"text":"x\nref","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":200.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"{ n: 1 }","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":92.0,"y1":40.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"z","x":200.0,"y":110.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"{ n: 2 }","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":300.0,"y":110.0,"text":"garbage","tone":"red","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":148.0,"text":"no references from roots — memory returns","size":9.0}]],"cues":[20.6,33.6]}]},{"title":"Errors","sub":"Exceptions at run time","short":"Errors","main":"Types aren't checked in advance: many errors surface at run time.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Kinds of errors","TypeError","try / catch"],"captions":["ReferenceError — no such variable, TypeError — wrong type, RangeError — value out of range","The familiar “Cannot read properties of undefined” means: the access chain stumbled on an empty value","Exceptions are caught with try and catch and thrown with throw; nobody checks types in advance"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":52.0,"text":"ReferenceError\nno such\nvariable","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":52.0,"text":"TypeError\nwrong operation\nfor the value","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":310.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":52.0,"text":"RangeError\nout of the\nallowed range","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let u;","u.name","// TypeError: Cannot read properties","//   of undefined (reading 'name')"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":40.0,"y":28.0,"lines":["try {","  JSON.parse('{');","} catch (e) {","  console.log(e.name);","}"],"hl":[3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":280.0},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":134.0,"w":160.0,"h":24.0,"text":"SyntaxError","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.9,30.1]}]},{"title":"Debugging","sub":"console and DevTools","short":"Debugging","main":"Check values and types at every step — don't guess.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["console","DevTools tabs","node --inspect"],"captions":["console.log prints values, console.table a table, console.error in red, debugger stops ex